1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,663
Before we ask Copilot to change a file, we
open Source Control and check the working

2
00:00:05,663 --> 00:00:08,008
tree on a disposable training branch.

3
00:00:08,188 --> 00:00:11,707
In this example, the repo begins with no
changes.

4
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:16,611
If you already have edits of your own,
identify them before an agent session so

5
00:00:16,611 --> 00:00:19,481
you can tell what came from the proposed
change.

6
00:00:19,661 --> 00:00:21,916
This gives us a baseline for review.

7
00:00:23,382 --> 00:00:27,669
The proposed diff changes the validator
and adds a regression test.

8
00:00:27,849 --> 00:00:31,913
It also includes an unrelated rename in a
training notes file.

9
00:00:32,093 --> 00:00:36,040
We inspect the exact lines instead of
relying on the summary.

10
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:39,454
The comparison and test line belong to
this issue.

11
00:00:39,634 --> 00:00:44,534
The notes change does not help meet the
acceptance criteria, so we will remove it

12
00:00:44,534 --> 00:00:46,470
before running the final checks.

13
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:53,339
Review the earlier failing run and confirm
the test failed for the specific boundary,

14
00:00:53,339 --> 00:00:54,995
because zero was accepted.

15
00:00:55,175 --> 00:00:59,953
Then rerun the suite with the corrected
condition in the approved environment.

16
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:03,779
We expect the zero test and the existing
tests to pass.

17
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:08,759
Use the same test command for both runs
and keep the evidence with the change.

18
00:01:10,215 --> 00:01:15,422
In Source Control, open the diff for the
training notes file and confirm that the

19
00:01:15,422 --> 00:01:17,607
edit came only from this exercise.

20
00:01:17,787 --> 00:01:22,932
Then discard that one file's change or
revert just the unwanted hunk with the

21
00:01:22,932 --> 00:01:24,603
available editor control.

22
00:01:24,783 --> 00:01:29,604
If the file contains work you want to
keep, revert only those specific lines.

23
00:01:29,784 --> 00:01:32,962
A broad discard can remove unrelated work.

24
00:01:34,423 --> 00:01:37,103
After undo, open Source Control again.

25
00:01:37,283 --> 00:01:41,495
The diff should now include only the
validator and the regression test.

26
00:01:41,675 --> 00:01:46,613
Run the suite once more if the recovery
touched the implementation or the tests.

27
00:01:46,793 --> 00:01:52,192
The post recovery check matters because an
undo action can affect more than intended

28
00:01:52,192 --> 00:01:54,057
if you pick the wrong target.

29
00:01:54,237 --> 00:01:57,269
Keep the changed files and test result
together.

30
00:01:58,715 --> 00:02:03,770
Some agent sessions offer a checkpoint or
a way to undo a proposed edit.

31
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:07,398
Check which files that action would
restore before using it.

32
00:02:07,578 --> 00:02:13,030
For a single unrelated hunk, a precise
editor undo often fits the work better.

33
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:18,061
For a session wide rollback in this
practice branch, first confirm the changes

34
00:02:18,061 --> 00:02:21,232
are contained and preserve any work you
still need.

35
00:02:22,673 --> 00:02:28,316
Practice on a sample branch that has one
correct change and one clearly identified

36
00:02:28,316 --> 00:02:29,073
extra edit.

37
00:02:29,253 --> 00:02:33,485
Keep the fix, undo the extra edit, and
review the resulting diff.

38
00:02:33,665 --> 00:02:36,089
Then explain the result in three parts.

39
00:02:36,269 --> 00:02:41,145
Describe the requirement, identify the
lines you kept, and show which tests

40
00:02:41,145 --> 00:02:42,381
verify the outcome.

41
00:02:42,561 --> 00:02:45,646
You now have evidence another developer
can review.
